  "method": "In-process MCP Client/InMemoryTransport; real production API and public SDK-default RPC reads; no signing or broadcast. A public example address is not a user-owned wallet claim.",
  "sampling": "Every call is represented. Duplicate text/structured JSON, calldata, wallet balances and most choice options are omitted. Character counts are serialized-envelope measurements, not token counts.",
  "instructions": "To move a token to the same asset on another chain, 1:1 less any partner fee: `sodax_bridge_tokens` lists what bridges between two chains, and `sodax_bridge_preview` shows what a bridge would deliver and the most its route takes now, building nothing. Once the user is ready to sign, call `sodax_bridge_prepare` with each side as the user names it (a chain plus a symbol, an address or \"native\") and their wallet as fromAddress (and the recipient as toAddress unless both chains are EVM): it returns the transactions to sign and the bridgeId. If a pair can't be bridged, it names the tokens that can. If it returns UNKNOWN_TOKEN, resolve that side with `sodax_resolve_token` with for: bridge and ask the user; never guess a token or an address. It doesn't check balances; `sodax_get_balance` with for: bridge reads them. Show the user the amounts and get their confirmation before their wallet signs; this server never signs or moves funds. Never pass private keys, seed phrases or API keys as tool inputs. After the user's wallet sends the bridge, call `sodax_bridge_submit_and_track` with the bridgeId and the bridge transaction's hash: it submits the bridge, so call it at least once, and never resend a bridge it hasn't reported failed. Every bridge tool result, errors included, carries nextAction: follow it until the result is terminal, or read its nextStep. If the user needs help with a swap or a bridge, they can ask the SODAX team on Discord, https://www.sodax.com/discord, giving the requestId from the tool result and any transaction hashes.",
  "tool_names": [
    "sodax_resolve_token",
    "sodax_get_balance",
    "sodax_bridge_tokens",
    "sodax_bridge_preview",
    "sodax_bridge_prepare",
